-- ISS-11212 (PLN-2122 Step 5): when a pull request's last comment reconcile
-- released its lease, complete or not. The comment-reconcile cron orders by it,
-- never-attempted first, so a pull request whose reconcile fails on every run
-- (no credential, a list at its page ceiling) no longer stays at the head of
-- the batch it used to fill. Nullable with no default: every existing row is
-- never-attempted, which is the order it already had. Generated by
-- `prisma migrate dev --create-only`.
--
-- The ADD COLUMN is a catalog change under ACCESS EXCLUSIVE on a table every
-- GitHub webhook writes, so the risk is lock QUEUEING behind a long open
-- transaction, with every writer queued behind it. `SET lock_timeout` bounds
-- that, as 20260903000000_iss8515 does: the migration fails fast and is
-- retried rather than stalling writes.
SET lock_timeout = '5s';

-- AlterTable
ALTER TABLE "pull_request_detail" ADD COLUMN     "comments_reconcile_attempted_at" TIMESTAMP(3);

RESET lock_timeout;
